# Pinned host keys for the hosts named in configs/ssh/config, read through
# UserKnownHostsFile alongside the regular known_hosts. A named host that
# presents a different key is refused even on a fresh machine, where
# StrictHostKeyChecking accept-new would otherwise trust whatever answers
# first. Public data. When a host is legitimately reinstalled, replace its
# lines here (ssh-keyscan <host>) and commit; tests/test_ssh.zsh requires an
# ed25519 entry for every named host.
172.16.188.128 ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIBkdaBTfm/NDIgq0rgivuwwkJpb5QmEFBhVwa76FpdsS
172.16.188.128 ssh-rsa 
192.168.1.178 ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIM2t90KGNlOq3AechfUmFc8FUhFAwkSc0f4RJSVi2pf5
192.168.1.178 ssh-rsa 
10.10.2.90 ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIJrsiIGctj5tBCnoFTtT5wwQ6RxzFVH2rbe9qdQj2k4M
10.10.2.90 ssh-rsa 
